<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49580" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tȳphōn</span></b>  (scanned
		Typhōn, Mart Cap. 2, 43), ōnis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>another name for the
				giart Typhōeus</i>, <i><span class="en">Luc. 4,
			595</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 92</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Ov. F 2, 461</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 2, 22</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 152</span></i>. Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tȳphōnĕus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Typhon</i>, <i>Typhonian</i>: specus, <i>the Typhon's cave</i> in
			Cilicia, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 13, 4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tȳphōnis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>daughter of Typhon</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Harpyiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 4, 428</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
